---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="About — JPX Web Development Co."
  description="Full-stack developer building websites and web applications for small businesses and nonprofits."
>
  <div class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-8">
    <section class="pt-24 pb-20 md:pt-32 md:pb-24">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="text-[40px] md:text-[62px] leading-[1.05] mt-8 max-w-[16ch]">
        I'm Ethan. <em class="em-accent">JPX is me.</em>
      </h1>
      <div class="rule mt-10"></div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-20 md:py-24" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--glass-line);">
      <div class="grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-[10rem_1fr]">
        <p class="eyebrow pt-2">The practice</p>

        <div class="prose-case max-w-[62ch]">
          <p>
            A full-stack developer building websites and web applications for small businesses and
            nonprofits — not templated marketing pages, but the infrastructure underneath:
            registration flows, admin dashboards, and the unglamorous plumbing that makes an
            organization's day-to-day actually work.
          </p>
          <p>
            This site is a fair example of how I work. I designed and built every part of it myself
            — the type system, the sliders on the In The Beginning card, the whole visual language —
            the same way I approach a client project: figure out exactly what it needs to do, then
            build it properly instead of reaching for a template.
          </p>
          <p>
            I work directly with the people I build for. No account managers, no outsourced backend,
            no handoff between "the developer" and "the person you actually talk to" — just one
            person who writes the code, tests it, and answers the phone after launch. If a project
            isn't a good fit, I'll say so upfront instead of taking it anyway.
          </p>
          <p>
            Small businesses and nonprofits get the same rate, the same code quality, and the same
            attention. I don't treat one as charity work and the other as the real job.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-20 md:py-24" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--glass-line);">
      <div class="grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-[10rem_1fr]">
        <p class="eyebrow pt-2">Next</p>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-7 flex-wrap">
          <a href="/contact" class="btn-neu">Book a 20-min call</a>
          <a class="link-ghost" href="/#work">See the work <span class="arr">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
